# Two reads of one list show the same rows: the first and the last row on the
# screen carry the same labels, and neither moved more than a few pixels - the
# rounding of a dump, not a swipe. A list with no row on the screen - one child
# larger than the list, a chart canvas, a picture - gives nothing to compare, and
# two such reads are not the same rows: they count as moved, and such a list runs
# to the safety net instead of reporting an end it never saw.
same_rows(){ local a b; set -- $1 $2
