usage(){ cat <<EOF
${B}yukti v$YUKTI_VERSION${R} — YUKTI — smart mobile-app QA automation for React Native / Expo

  yukti doctor              check/guide the toolchain (Xcode, node@22, cocoapods, idb)
  yukti init                write a starter yukti.config.json
  yukti scan                list device-only frameworks (no arm64-sim slice) to exclude
  yukti build <variant>     build a signed arm64 simulator .app (local)
  yukti pull  <variant>     pull an OFFICIAL simulator build from EAS (needs EXPO_TOKEN)
  yukti boot                create/boot the simulator
  yukti up    <variant>     build + boot + install + launch  (one shot)
  yukti install <variant> [--apk <path>]
                            install a build; on Android --apk (or the variant's
                            "apkPath") installs an APK built elsewhere, e.g. by CI
  yukti flow  <file.json>   run a deterministic flow (Talos test-case engine — no AI, CI-ready)
                            leaves \$YUKTI_RESULTS_DIR/<flow>.xml (JUnit) — per-step result
  yukti flow --check <file.json>
                            build the flow and stop: verbs, keys, conditions,
                            includes and variables, no device, nothing performed

  drive primitives (for flows or an AI agent — Claude Code / OpenAI):
  yukti shot [file]         screenshot the sim (an agent reads the PNG)
  yukti ui                  accessibility tree (JSON, coords in points)
  yukti find "<label>"      -> "x y" center of the first element matching label
  yukti tap <x> <y>         tap
  yukti type "<text>"       type (char-by-char = reliable; idb bulk-type drops chars)
  yukti clear <x> <y>       clear a text field
  yukti scroll <up|down|left|right>
                            scroll the screen · yukti scroll-to "<label>" [dir] [clear] scroll a label into view, fail on a miss
  yukti dismiss             auto-dismiss common modals (Not Now / Skip / OK / Close…)
  yukti assert "<text>"     assert the text is on screen (perceivable text only, no scroll)
  yukti stop-app <variant>  force-stop the app of that variant
  yukti clear-state <variant>
                            wipe the app's data (Android only) - the app stops, launch it again
  yukti open-url "<key>"    open a screen of the app under test by its key ("home", "cart")
                            the app of \$YUKTI_VARIANT; the address is that variant's "urlBase"
                            plus the key, or plus its path from the "urls" table when there is
                            one, so no flow carries an environment. It delivers the address,
                            and arrival is asynchronous - the step after it is a waitFor
  yukti wait-for "<text>" [s] [exact|contains]
                            poll until the text is on screen, fail on timeout (default 10s)
  yukti tap-id "<id>"       tap the element with this a11y id / resource-id segment
  yukti clear-id "<id>"     empty the text field with this a11y id / resource-id segment
  yukti assert-id "<id>"    assert an element with this id is on screen
  yukti assert-box "<q>" <assert|id> minWidth=48dp minHeight=48dp
                            assert the box of that element: minWidth, minHeight,
                            maxWidth, maxHeight, minX, minY, maxX, maxY, written
                            in pixels (48), dp ("48dp") or a share ("5%")
  yukti assert-not "<text>" assert the text is NOT on the current screen (no scroll)
  yukti assert-not-id "<id>"
                            assert no element with this id is on the current screen

  flow steps: wait · waitFor · waitForId · screenshot · tap · tapText · optionalTapText · tapId · scroll · scrollToText · dismiss · type · clearText · clearTextId · pressKey · hideKeyboard · assertText · assertId · assertNotText · assertNotId · assertBox · assertBoxId · launch · stopApp · clearState · openUrl · include
              (clearText · clearTextId · pressKey · hideKeyboard · assertBox · assertBoxId: measured on Android, iOS not yet run)
              stopApp force-stops the app, clearState wipes its data (Android only); both take the variant name
              openUrl takes the key of a screen, not an address: the address is the variant's "urlBase" plus the key
